From a78f977ef58c9ef0e7ad8ea2425031fc5970372a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] test(goldens): post NC goldens only for programs the gate
 passes

contour_disc_hole and contour_tangential_lead used 3 mm leads on the
R6 bore, whose r = 3 cutter-centre ring is the lead circle itself: the
leads crossed the ring and the gate refused both programs, yet their
posted NC goldens sat in every dialect. The leads are now 2 mm, inside
the ring, and both programs verify clean; their CL goldens and the 16
posted NC goldens (Fanuc top + 7 dialects) are regenerated - only the
lead coordinates move, every file keeps its line count.

The refusal stays pinned on its own fixture
(a_lead_on_the_rings_own_circle_is_refused, the old crossing pairs),
and every_posted_golden_is_a_program_the_gate_passes walks every .nc
golden under tests/golden/nc/ so a refused program can no longer be
posted as a golden (or must say so on its first line). The plate
builders move to tests/common/solid_part.rs (400-line law).

Fixes #862

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
